cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below, and cite the book it accompanies."
title: "Deep Learning with Python: A Practical and Mathematical Introduction — Companion Code"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Every program printed in the book Deep Learning with Python: A Practical and
  Mathematical Introduction (Nitin Rakesh, Viraj Gulhane and Shreyas Hole,
  2026), organized chapter by chapter under the file names the book uses, with
  the expected output of each program, a Jupyter/Colab notebook per chapter,
  and the scripts that generate the book's figures. The programs cover the
  mathematics of neural networks implemented from scratch in NumPy,
  backpropagation, optimizers and regularization, PyTorch and Keras, CNNs,
  RNNs, LSTMs and GRUs, attention and Transformers, NLP, autoencoders, GANs,
  diffusion models, object detection, segmentation, time series,
  explainability and responsible AI, and deployment.
keywords:
  - deep learning
  - neural networks
  - machine learning
  - Python
  - PyTorch
  - Keras
  - NumPy
  - textbook
  - education
authors:
